sequenceDiagram
  %% status: draft
  %% command: POST /api/v1/conn/launches
  %% kind: conn.launch
  autonumber
  participant C as API caller
  participant G as Gateway
  participant S as Swamp
  C->>G: Admit the launch
  %%> Validate the expected device and its locked profile binding on first admission and replay.
  %%> Store the encrypted request with the parent Operation.
  G-->>C: 202 · launch snapshot
  G->>S: Prepare the Instance
  %%> Use the exact owned create or admitted wake. Record application completion separately.
  %%> On explicit Retry, admit a fresh wake if the existing Instance slept again. Wait for it before probing T3 again.
  %%> Read the registered stock T3 project and model defaults.
  alt Cancel wins the Operation lock
    %% path: cancel
    G->>S: Remove owned work
    %%> Check the clone for work and T3 activity even when its create failed.
    %%> Lock the Instance and check for other launches before admitting teardown.
    %%> If the owned removal stopped the container before it failed, retry that removal using the recorded stop result.
    %%> Verified cleanup ends the launch. A failed or unproven cleanup remains Cancelling.
    S-->>G: Cleanup proof
  else Dispatch wins the Operation lock
    %% path: handoff
    G->>S: Send the first message
    %%> After an ambiguous reply, read the exact message on the original T3 state.
    S-->>G: Verified acceptance
    Note over G: Publish the thread
    %%> Retry only publication after acceptance. Leave a deleted workspace absent.
  end
  C->>G: Follow or control
  G-->>C: Recorded snapshot
